data/repair_backups/

# pytest tmp_path spill: a run with a cwd-relative --basetemp writes dirs named
# `test_<test_name><n>` at the repo root. Legit test code lives in tests/, so a
# root-anchored guard cannot hide anything real and keeps them out of `git add -A`.
/test_*/

# One-off root probes and benches. These are throwaway connection/dimension
# diagnostics, not part of the product; `testpaths = tests` means the two
# `test_*.py` entries never run under pytest, but they were committed by
# accident (f461779b) and stayed in the tree. Root-anchored so a future module
# of the same name under src/ is unaffected.
/bench_common.py
/diag_conn.py
/probe_*.py
/verify_dim256.py
/test_db_conn.py
/test_nemotron.py
